  "Question": "Ara and Shea were once the same height. Since then Shea has grown \\(20\\%\\) while Ara has grown half as many inches as Shea. Shea is now \\(60\\) inches tall. How tall, in inches, is Ara now?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(48\\)",
    "B": "\\(51\\)",
    "C": "\\(52\\)",
    "D": "\\(54\\)",
    "E": "\\(55\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Shea's \\(20\\%\\) growth was measured from the original height. Therefore Shea's current height is \\(120\\%\\), or \\(1.2\\) times, that original height. Dividing by this factor gives their common original height:\n\\[\n60\\div1.2=50\\text{ inches}.\n\\]\nShea has grown \\(60-50=10\\) inches. Ara has grown half as many inches, which is \\(\\frac12\\cdot10=5\\) inches. Ara is therefore now \\(50+5=\\boxed{55}\\) inches tall, choice E.",
